[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139203,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyxoma is a benign mesenchymal tumour comprising spindle or stellate cells and thin-walled arborizing vessels in a myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139204,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8841/0 Angiomyxoma</p>\r\n<p>8841/0 Cutaneous myxoma (superficial angiomyxoma)</p>\r\n<p>8841/0 Aggressive angiomyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139205,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F7C &amp; XH9HK9 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Angiomyxoma</p>\r\n<p>2E84.0 &amp; XH58A9 Benign fibrogenic or myofibrogenic tumour of skin &amp; Superficial angiomyxoma</p>\r\n<p>2F7C &amp; XH4V74 Neoplasms of uncertain behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Deep angiomyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139206,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable</em>: for superficial angiomyxoma: cutaneous myxoma; for deep angiomyxoma: aggressive angiomyxoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139207,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxoma; deep (aggressive) angiomyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139208,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxomas occur in the conjunctiva {29631843} and eyelids {32495538;15953464}; deep angiomyxomas occur in the soft tissues of the orbit {20562663;17467533}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139209,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Eyelid angiomyxomas present as multinodular, polypoid, or pedunculated slow-growing dermal/subcutaneous masses involving the eyelid margin {15953464;21708097;32495538}. In the conjunctiva, they appear as well-circumscribed, fleshy masses {29631843}. Orbital angiomyxomas present with proptosis and visual disturbances {20562663;17467533}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139210,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyxomas arise in patients across a wide age range, but predominantly in the third to fifth decades of life {32495538;29631843;21708097;20562663;17467533}, with no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139211,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Multiple superficial angiomyxomas may be seen in Carney complex, an autosomal dominant syndrome with germline mutation in <em>PRKAR1A </em>encoding a PKA subunit {15371594}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139212,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyxomas of the eye region have not been reported to be associated with Carney complex, although it is suspected that <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivation may play a role in the pathogenesis of sporadic tumours given the lack of protein expression on immunohistochemistry in 80% of cases {26130139;34532875}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139213,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiomyxomas form poorly circumscribed, lobulated masses with a gelatinous surface {32495538;20562663}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139214,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Superficial angiomyxomas are poorly circumscribed, forming lobules separated by collagenous septa, composed of spindle-shaped to stellate cells with bland ovoid nuclei in an abundant myxoid and variably collagenous stroma {32495538;20562663;29631843}. Thin-walled non-arborizing vessels are prominent {31078543;32495538;17467533}. Stromal neutrophils may be seen {15953464;21708097}.</p>\r\n<p>Deep angiomyxomas have increased cellularity and thick-walled vessels showing medial hypertrophy and perivascular hyalinization {20562663}.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>Tumour cells express vimentin and CD34, and are negative for S100, desmin, SMA, and cytokeratins {32495538}. There is loss of PRKAR1A expression, particularly in Carney complex&ndash;associated lesions {31078543}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes nerve sheath myxoma (S100 positive) {33403177}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139215,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139216,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139217,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> hypocellular, myxoid, lobulated tumour; bland stellate to spindle-shaped cells; non-arborizing capillary-like vasculature.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139218,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139219,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Complete excision with wide margins is recommended {29631843;20562663}. There is frequent recurrence (30&ndash;40%) due to infiltrative growth and the inability to excise completely, requiring prolonged follow-up {3389450;21708097;17467533;20562663}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]